<header><p class="eyebrow">November 13, 2026 · Men and women · Authenticated owner result</p><h1>Preflight failed.<br>Prior scientific work is preserved.</h1><p class="intro">The latest B063R4 return stopped during recovery before a new worker started. A missing Python process-handle API caused the failure. B063R5 addresses that compatibility gap and preserves the diagnostic evidence needed to verify the next owner attempt.</p></header>
<div class="cards" id="r5-cards"><div class="card"><strong>0</strong><span>New fits in the actual B063R4 attempt</span></div><div class="card"><strong>22</strong><span>Prior target fits preserved<br>134 exact objects reverified</span></div><div class="card"><strong>Failed</strong><span>Authenticated preflight result</span></div><div class="card"><strong>Unverified</strong><span>B063R5 owner execution<br>and older owner shutdown</span></div></div>
<aside class="notice" id="r5-scope"><p><strong>The failure return does not contain new scientific results.</strong> It confirms zero new owner fits. It does not establish that the older R3 owner stopped successfully, and its referenced recovery diagnostic was not included.</p><p>The earlier <a href="b063r4.html">dated R3 progress and R4 preparation report</a> remains intact. Its recorded fits and CPU observations belong to that earlier evidence period. The latest failure cannot turn them into R4 execution or twelve-core acceptance.</p></aside>
<section id="r5-failure"><h2>What the return proves—and what remains unknown</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>A missing Python binding stopped recovery</h3><p>The exact failure code is <code>B065_PIDFD_REQUIRED_FOR_PROCESS_CONTROL</code>. The returned implementation checks for Python process-handle bindings before attempting a kernel operation. At least one binding was absent.</p><p class="muted">The return does not identify the individual missing binding or provide the owner's Python, kernel or C runtime versions. It does not prove that the kernel lacks process-handle support.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Preservation carries no new-fit credit</h3><p>All <strong>134 saved content objects</strong> supporting the <strong>22 prior target fits</strong> were authenticated again inside the returned source. This review did not deserialize models or rerun science.</p><p class="muted">Admission still requires exact scientific, input and runtime compatibility. Preserving an artifact does not automatically make it compatible with a different Python or package environment.</p></article></div><details id="r5-clocks"><summary>Inspect the evidence clock and diagnostic gap</summary><p>The return filename contains <time datetime="2026-11-13T01:33:34Z">November 13, 2026 at 01:33:34 UTC</time>. This is a filename timestamp, not a verified failure completion time. No new forecast issue time or outcome clock is inferred from it.</p><p>The source, nested return and all declared archive members were verified against their recorded hashes. The failure text references a recovery diagnostic that is absent from the attached return. Successful old-owner shutdown and the actual failed capability details remain unverified.</p></details></section>
<section id="r5-repair"><h2>The scoped engineering repair</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Portable, identity-safe process handles</h3><p>When a Python binding is missing, use typed interfaces to the same kernel process-handle operations. Verify the descriptor's target and the complete process identity before signaling. Close each acquired descriptor.</p><p>Errors from an existing callable API remain failures. The repair does not substitute another route after a permission denial, kernel refusal or unsupported-operation error.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Early capability evidence and portable diagnostics</h3><p>A fresh, nonterminating self probe records the actual Python bindings, kernel, C runtime and selected backend before recovery work. Recovery evidence belongs in the returned diagnostic, where the next review can authenticate it.</p><p>Engineering tests and a source fingerprint establish prepared code. Actual owner recovery, science and throughput still require a new owner return.</p></article></div><details id="r5-engineering"><summary>Inspect validation and the prepared source fingerprint</summary><p id="r5-tests">__B063R5_TESTS__</p><p>Prepared B063R5 source fingerprint: <code id="r5-source">__B063R5_SOURCE__</code>.</p><p>Local compatibility checks force missing Python bindings and exercise real, nonterminating kernel probes. Refusal and descriptor-cleanup cases protect the process boundary. These checks are engineering verification, with zero scientific-fit credit.</p></details></section>
<section id="r5-remaining"><h2>The scientific obligations remain open</h2><ol><li>Verify the old owner's safe exit or authenticated terminal evidence, then admit a new owner.</li><li>Demonstrate actual independent scientific fits, sustained utilization and comparable throughput across all 12 safely available project cores.</li><li>Complete eligible historical evaluation and current-season/upcoming game coverage with exact issue and outcome clocks.</li><li>Report accuracy, log loss, Brier, margin MAE/RMSE and total-points MAE/RMSE, with separate former, current and rolling champions and genuine time-matched provider data.</li></ol><p>No new metrics, forecasts, DraftKings quotes, Kalshi quotes or Polymarket quotes were created by this incident update. The retained dashboard keeps its original dated populations and coverage qualifications.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="index.html">Open preserved NCAA dashboard</a><a href="b063r4.html">Inspect prior saved progress</a><a id="r5-download" href="data/B063R5_PUBLIC_STATUS.json" download>Download exact status JSON</a></div></section>
<footer id="r5-publication">Sanitized NCAA operational evidence. Source publication is separate from website deployment and does not imply a provider refresh or new scientific evaluation. Exact fingerprints and the distinction between the failed owner attempt and prepared repair are in the downloadable JSON.</footer>
